{
  "about": "Terrain and map features: movement, cover, sight and durability (docs/map-design.md). A hex has one ground and at most one hex object; lines (walls, hedges, fences, sandbags, wire) are polylines compiled to hex edges; structures are buildings with a footprint (every building can be destroyed; map production buildings are structures of kind production, CoH3 HP 1500, or production_heavy, 2000; HQ HP and rebuild cost from CoH3); wrecks are placed when vehicles and emplacements die; units of a wreck_clearing role clear one by spending their action on clear_turns turns (design values). cost: move points to enter (per move class), cross: extra points to cross an edge; null = impassable. sight: none | partial | block. height 0–3. Movement and sight values from v214; durability values are Burning Front design values except defensive features, which take HP and armour from the faction's CoH3 entity (faction_ebps; neutral = placed by the map).",
